<div>
  <p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>If you are 18 or older, the payout account is verified in your own name. If you are 13 to 17 and your account country is the United States, you keep the account in your name and add a parent or legal guardian, who is verified instead of you. See <a href="#sellers-under-18">Sellers under 18</a>. Outside the United States, the account holder must be 18 or older.</li>
    <li>Use your full legal name (including any middle name) and/or full business name.</li>
    <li>Must use a physical address, no PO boxes. If a P.O. Box is the only address on your business or government documents, see <a href="13-getting-paid#Address-verification-dK7mR">Address verification</a>. The document cannot match the account, so support has to help you sort it out.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Changing your country?</strong> Save the country change by itself first. Your payout and identity details are tied to your country, so changing it clears your saved bank account, name, date of birth, address, and tax details. After the country update finishes, return to this page, re-enter your payout and identity details, and save again.</p>
  <h3>Choosing your account type</h3>
  <p>First, choose how you will operate – either as an individual or as a business:</p>
  <figure><%= image_tag "https://d33v4339jhl8k0.cloudfront.net/docs/assets/5c4657ad2c7d3a66e32d763f/images/63b6b07ebfe3f971fb093bce/file-IGvUdtWuhl.png" %></figure>
  <p>Choose ‘Individual’ if you operate under your name (effectively as a sole proprietor) or do not have business registration documents. </p>
  <p>Conversely, choose ‘Business’ if you already have business registration documents. </p>
  <p>For businesses, the person on the Gumroad account acts as the ‘business representative’ and will need to submit registration documents and personal identification details, as well.</p>
  <h3>A. Identity verification (for bank payouts)</h3>
  <p>*If you only see PayPal as your payout option, skip to B.</p>
  <p>Gumroad uses <a href="http://www.stripe.com/">Stripe</a> to process all credit card payments and bank payouts, and we are subject to Stripe’s policies and regulations. Stripe is required to follow <a href="https://support.stripe.com/questions/know-your-customer-obligations">Know Your Customer obligations</a> which tailor account verifications by country. </p>
  <p>At some point, Stripe will request several of the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your date of birth, legal name, phone number, and address</li>
    <li>A government ID number (e.g., SSN or your country’s national ID)</li>
    <li>A scan or image of your photo ID (passport, driver’s license, or ID). <a href="https://support.stripe.com/questions/passport-id-or-drivers-license-upload-requirement">Read why.</a></li>
    <li>Company Tax ID and business registration document (if applicable)</li>
    <li>Proof of home address (recent utility bill, bank statement, rental agreement, etc.)</li>
    <li>Phone number</li>
  </ul>
  <p>All information added and uploaded to Gumroad is encrypted and passed to Stripe for verification purposes. Unless you need help and email us your ID, Gumroad’s team will never see your submitted documents or banking information, nor will those be exposed to 3rd parties.</p>
  <h3>US tax ID numbers</h3>
  <p>If you're <a href="https://support.stripe.com/questions/tax-id-verification-guidelines-by-business-type-in-the-us">in the USA</a>, your Tax ID is usually the Employer Identification Number (EIN) assigned by the IRS. For individuals/sole proprietorships, you can provide your SSN if you don't have an EIN. For additional information on what name and TIN to provide, please see instructions on the <a href="https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/fw9.pdf">IRS Form W-9</a>.</p>
  <p>For other countries, you can go through the list of Tax IDs accepted by our payment processor (Stripe) <a href="https://stripe.com/docs/tax/tax-ids#supported-tax-ids">here</a>.</p>
  <h3>B. Identity verification (for PayPal payouts)</h3>
  <p>If you don't have bank payouts in your settings, simply add your name, address, phone number, and active PayPal account email. You do not need to submit an ID or other documents for PayPal payouts.</p>
  <p>Both personal and business PayPal accounts are acceptable.</p>
  <h3 id="sellers-under-18">Sellers under 18</h3>
  <p>Gumroad accounts are available from age 13, but a payout account has to be verified against an adult. If you are 13 to 17 and your account country is the United States, you can still get paid: the Gumroad account, the products, and the payouts stay in your name, and you add a parent or legal guardian in payout settings. Stripe, our payment processor, verifies the guardian instead of you.</p>
  <p>Your guardian provides their own full legal name, date of birth, home address, and the last four digits of their Social Security Number, and accepts Stripe's terms. If Stripe cannot verify them automatically, it may ask for their full SSN and then a scan of their photo ID. Their details are used only for this verification.</p>
  <p>This is available for United States accounts. Stripe does not offer a guardian path in every country, so if your account country is outside the United States, the account holder must be 18 or older. We will add more countries as Stripe confirms support for them.</p>
  <h3>Frequently asked questions: </h3>
  <p><strong>Q: Can I choose not to enter my information into the payout settings?</strong></p>
  <p>A: No. You must fill out the payout settings.</p>
  <p><strong>Q: Can I change from bank payouts to PayPal payouts?</strong></p>
  <p>A: No.</p>
